  "definitions": [
    "Primary, answer support: the judge sees the question, gold answer, gold sentences as one reference route, and the items. It quotes a chain to the gold answer by the reference route or any route the items state, says whether the chain is complete, and whether the answer is stated, only mentioned, or missing.",
    "Support score: 3 complete verified chain and answer stated (yes/no answers: complete chain); 2 answer stated; 1 answer mentioned or some verified chain quote; 0 otherwise. Support score % = sum / (3 x questions) x 100; full support rate = share scoring 3.",
    "Secondary, gold-sentence recall, as follows.",
    "Gold sentences are split into claims once per question; every method is judged against the same frozen claims.",
    "Each claim is stated, missing, or contradicted; stated and contradicted need a quote that appears verbatim (after normalization) in the cited item, otherwise the claim counts as missing.",
    "Gold sentence score: 3 all claims stated; 2 main claim stated; 1 people or things mentioned or a minor claim stated; 0 otherwise. Any verified contradiction scores 0.",
    "Question score: the lowest gold sentence score.",
    "Retrieval score: sum of question scores / (3 x questions) x 100.",
    "Full retrieval rate: share of questions scoring 3, x 100.",
    "Budget view: ranked methods cut to Agentic GraphRAG's per-question token volume (as in retrieval_quality); quotes outside the cut do not count.",
    "Judge sees no method name, no question, and items in a seeded shuffle.",
    "Intervals are paired percentile bootstraps over the same questions."
  ],
